0 -240.1164 Td
(Problem Description)Tj
/F0 10 Tf
0 -24 Td
(In this project, the study of methods and techniques to analyse malicious code will be performed.)Tj
0 -12 Td
(How to combine techniques in order to detect different flavours of malware, as well as how to)Tj
0 -12 Td
(automate \(parts of\) the analysis process will be emphasized.)Tj
0 -24 Td
(The primary focus will be on the analysis of binary code in the form of PE or PE+, but it is believed)Tj
0 -12 Td
(that other file formats will require more or less the same techniques and the project could of)Tj
0 -12 Td
(course be extended to include other file formats running on other platforms than Microsoft's. The)Tj
0 -12 Td
(system will use VMWare virtualization software as an emulator and virtual environment in which)Tj
0 -12 Td
(to run the malicious samples. Virtualization technology supported by processors, such Intel)Tj
0 -12 Td
(Virtualization Technology \(IVT\) and AMD Virtualization \(AMD-V or Pacifica\), enables isolation at the)Tj
0 -12 Td
(hardware level.)Tj
0 -24 Td
(As approximately 90% of all malware is distributed in a packed form, typically by using runtime)Tj
0 -12 Td
(packers such as UPX or ASPACK, it would be desirable to unpack the target code to ease the)Tj
0 -12 Td
(process of analysis.)Tj
0 -36 Td
(Assignment given: 23. January 2007)Tj
0 -12 Td
(Supervisor: Svein Johan Knapskog, ITEM)Tj
